#Lab enviroment

## Objective

The objective of this is to set up the virtual machinces for this lab.
This project will use a Windows 11 vm for blue team testing and Kali Linux vm for red team testing.

## Virtual Machines

|VM Name | Operating System | Role | CPU | Ram | Storage |
|Sentinel| Windows 11 | Blue Team | 4 CPU | 5000mb | 80GB |
|Raider| Kali Linux | Red Team | 4 CPU | 5000mb | 20GB |

## Windows VM Setup

- Download Windows ISO 
- In VirtualBox select New
- VM Name, mount ISO in ISO Image, verifiy OS and OS Version
- set Username and password
- Finish settings seen above
- VM downloads and boots.


## Kali Linux

- Download Kali Linux ISO from kali.org
- In VirtualBox select New
- VM Name, mount ISO in ISO Image, OS selected Debian, OS Version Debian 64-bit
- Settings seen above
- Start machine 
- Press ENTER on graphical interface 
- configure +language, country, keyboard language, Hostname- Raider, Domain Name- lab.local, Username- raider, password, clock
- Guided - use entire disk, all files, write changes to disk- yes
- Software Desktop, Xfce, collection tools, top 10, default
- GRUB Boot loader yes, choose Box for installation 
- Succesful Boot 

